+# T179-Pd pre-P0 history DESIGN review — conditional direction; engineering blocked
+
+Reviewed candidate `35950488c3bd12241384dca9c13cd3166d738fb9`, exact parent/base `e312c78b3f1a95766f535ef8372b049ee550138c`. Consultation source baseline `8b3acffd4a75d58b7b86bc6baade1e994d3ae5e3`. Requested/configured independent reviewer: GPT-6 Astra / XHigh; serving-backend telemetry is unavailable. Repository read-only; source/Git/text/hash inspection only. No build, discovery, tests, application execution, network, fetch/push or delegation.
+
+**The proposal is a substantive, source-supported direction for conditional discussion. It is not a complete engineering contract or a pre-P0 recovery release.** One confirmed design branch defect requires correction before engineering (PH-D01 below). The already declared R01–R08 are real unresolved owner/protocol dependencies, not completed work. Nothing in this review restricts the separately accepted narrow observed-reader implementation; its current edits/tests/runtime are excluded.
+
+## PH-D01 — choose legacy dispatch from the original contract, not the request alone
+
+**Severity: medium, confirmed specification defect; no implemented runtime defect claimed.** Location: proposal `Version-first cold reader`, line 173 (step 2), with lines 71–79 and step 3 at 174.
+
+Step 2 currently states “Old unversioned request -> existing old route” before step 3 checks the original-issued seed. That branch is broader than the proposal's own original-selected lifecycle. Consider an intact newly versioned original whose request/control is accidentally replaced by an old-format same-session/request/turn repair request, or a partial migration that leaves an old writer/cleanup consumer active. The request is unversioned and correlated, but the original still requires durable history. Following step 2 literally selects Legacy without checking that obligation, permitting dispatch or cleanup through the old transport behavior and losing the versioned history requirement. Existing tuple-based consumers make this a meaningful boundary: daemon correlation at `game_master_daemon.ps1:4294–4312` and the ordinary reader's context matching do not establish the new origin/history contract. No hostile-edit or cryptographic threat assumption is needed.
+
+Required correction: after native debt settlement and actual original/G validation, derive the lifecycle mode from the authenticated original's supported seed/version (and genuine terminal disposition where applicable). Return Legacy only when that original/context is genuinely eligible for the unchanged old protocol. A versioned original paired with missing, unversioned, unknown-version, wrong-kind, malformed or foreign control is SourceConflict/MissingOwnerProof or a specifically proved terminal settlement; it is never an implicit legacy downgrade. Conversely a versioned control cannot upgrade an old/no-seed original. A control's discriminator selects its parser, not the original's protocol obligations. Apply this matrix consistently to dispatch, correlation, validation and cleanup, not only the cold reader.
+
+Finite future cases: (1) genuine old original + old request retains old behavior; (2) genuine new original + valid new control uses the new lifecycle; (3) new original + same-tuple old request refuses before dispatch/cleanup; (4) new original + missing/unknown/malformed control retains evidence; (5) old original + new control cannot mint history; (6) terminal deletion requires actual terminal/original/M3 proof. These are UNRUN. This is a concrete correction within R02, not a requirement to add a pathname or revise the trusted-local threat model.
+
+## Source claims independently supported
+
+- **Original preparation is not already the proposed completion transaction.** `GameEngine.SessionAndSnapshots.cs:398–420, 514–569` builds a real original and writes manifest then authority sequentially; artifacts precede them. `BrowserPlayerInput.cs:198–227` has its own provisional request, staged proof/publication and original seal. The proposal correctly requires a new actual ordinary/browser completion relation before claiming original-pair-plus-control atomicity; merely grouping three JSON objects in a helper would not supply it. The seed-to-control hash direction is acyclic: original seed first, finished original hashes in control. No rewriting of already-issued originals is acceptable.
+- **The current repair request is disposable transport.** `ValidationAndRepair.cs:4048, 4149–4177` deletes previous controls, may complete a worker branch, and only later writes the old request if needed. Success/cancellation and `DeleteValidationRepairFiles:8290–8295` remove these files. `ReportRejectedRepairReadyAsync:8146–8169` rewrites transport from Ready errors rather than preserving the complete previous canonical issue basis. The proposal correctly distinguishes owner issue history from transport revisions.
+- **Freshness needs actual historical facts.** The actual start sample at `ValidationAndRepair.cs:354`, request DetectedAtUtc at 4078, merged canonical state at 369–389 and target/fallback policy at 2688–2784 are separate. Missing, metadata-error and older-than-start targets can require an actual fallback sample; output freshness uses strict greater-than. Storing only request timestamps or the latest visible error list cannot reproduce these relations. Raw validation has its own route/sample, so a canonical-only ledger would be incomplete.
+- **Restoration and Ready consumption have real crash cuts.** `WaitForContractRepairAsync:3322` restores before dispatch for applicable packets. `SessionAndSnapshots.cs:2091–2127` distinguishes the joint restore and ordinary restore plus an optional pending checkpoint. `ValidationAndRepair.cs:3558–3567` appends diagnostics, deletes Ready and returns before the caller later derives freshness. These facts support R03 and the proposed exact atomic submitted/Ready-consumption transition; existing helper completion is not already such a receipt.
+- **Worker apply, audit and Ready are distinct.** `GmWorkerApplyGate.cs:306–376` begins one complete B1 intended set, validates ownership and commits before returning Accepted. Audit in `ApplyReservedAsync:128–139` follows that outcome. `GmWorkerValidationRepairDelegator.cs:223–280` applies first and separately publishes Ready, preserving only hot decision/task/proposal data on uncertainty. A fixed client-owned companion in the initial B1 set is a plausible way to retain the application fact atomically, but audit/post-return bookkeeping is not a substitute. Zero changed files currently skip the transaction, while `FileSystemManager.WorkerPublication.cs:16` rejects an empty set; the proposed zero-change companion is a real apply-owner extension.
+- **Cold worker authority is genuinely open.** `GmWorkerDurableExecution.cs:7–9` excludes minting the retained live authority from persisted fields or a replacement process. `GmWorkerTaskRunResult` derives validation from its internal ExecutionAuthority (`GmWorkerModels.cs:458–468`). `GmWorkerBridgePool.TryReserveTaskAsync:1270–1321` rejects existing task/inbox artifacts. Task identity/latest-task preparation and actual reservation are separate. The proposed distinct cold disposition must neither deserialize that live capability nor call RunTaskAsync with a saved ID as an assumed resume.
+- **All-consumer work is substantive.** The daemon uses request presence/write time for dispatch and root tuple correlation; the helper reads root request fields and publishes Ready. `InactiveSnapshotEvidence.cs:176–185` treats request presence as a retention blocker; `MortalJointTerminalCleanup.cs:247–253` expects the old tuple and full-turn flag; SaveLoad excludes this pathname and original evidence as ephemeral. Versioned history therefore changes more than a private field. Explicit non-dispatch states and same-change guidance/examples/guards are necessary. Same-root crash recovery must not be mislabeled as qualified distinct-root in-flight archive recovery.
+
+These source facts support examining the existing request pathname as one candidate. They do not prove it is globally minimal in engineering cost or establish a need for any additional pathname. “Smallest found” is a scoped architectural judgment, not measured complexity or a necessity theorem.
+
+## What is sound in the conditional direction
+
+The proposal keeps final frozen evidence in existing M3, avoids mutable history in an already-issued original and avoids an informal prepublished completed M. It distinguishes client-owned history from worker ChangedFiles. A staged worker_applied companion is correctly not proof while the B1 decision is pending; hot validation and cold readers must honor the real pending-decision owner. The committed companion plus independent task/proposal/scope/after-image semantics can be a durable application observation under the existing trusted-local model without minting a live worker permit.
+
+Leaving frozen control unchanged as a pre-seal guard and letting verified M3 establish handoff avoids an unnecessary split transferred acknowledgement. Exact control/source guards and evidence must already participate before common input/preparation/cache/take seals. The existing pathname does not implicitly expand write membership. Any alternate control mutation in common needs its actual owner, member and seal relation designed explicitly.
+
+The distinction between durable observations and lost in-memory work is correct. A crash can lose a sampled UTC or allocated identity before persistence; a history filename cannot recover it. An unfinished read-only attempt could only be restarted under an expressly chosen no-publication/source/policy contract. It must not replace a frozen sample, reschedule source mechanics, allocate replacement identities for accepted work, or replay the player's action/committed consequences. The proposal correctly leaves both this choice and the stronger lost-C/result policy open.
+
+Named historical samples remain client-owned observation facts under trusted-local SHA256-PAYLOAD-JSON semantics, not cryptographic proof against coordinated rewriting. Cold checkers must derive all available semantic relations; a persisted success flag, self-hash, predecessor hash or plausible receipt alone is insufficient. “Semantic tamper rejected” should retain this relational meaning, not universal historical attestation of irrecoverable clock samples.
+
+## Dependencies that prevent engineering release
+
+The proposal explicitly acknowledges these; they are not additional surprise findings:
+
+1. **R01/R03:** exact original preparation and restoration completion protocols, including browser recorder boundaries, full artifact/cohort proof, optional pending state, cuts before/after acknowledgement and deterministic actual recovery disposition. No repeat possibly committed restore because a history acknowledgement is absent.
+2. **R02:** closed tagged rows, required/null tables, transition adjacency, protocol-mode matrix (PH-D01), real retry/transport identity, original/seed/payload schemas and a complete consumer-purpose map. Current phase names and conceptual APIs do not define those bytes. A repair wait retains private/durable state, never a canonical lease across GM work.
+3. **R04:** actual reservation/launch/publication/cold execution settlement, live versus cold permit separation, same-B1 client companion preparation and zero-change handling. A published-but-unapplied proposal needs a genuine cold apply admission or proved retirement plus lawful fallback; neither is currently chosen/proved. Pending companion visibility during existing validation must be treated as proposed owner state, never committed acceptance.
+4. **R05:** exact pure source/classification/freshness/comparison/worker outcome checkers, complete original/G/source/tuple binding and source closure. Persisting all observations does not itself make full validation pure or independently checkable.
+5. **R06:** an explicit policy for unfinished observation attempts and hot C/result/identity loss. Durable prepared result/identity commitment plus its checker, or an explicitly justified abandonment of an uncommitted effect-free attempt, must be selected and qualified. This review selects neither option.
+6. **R07:** no-publication/attempt/debt classification, actual same-candidate common/native settlement, full cold M3/cohort semantics and terminal retention/retirement. Absent M is not “never attempted”; frozen history is not a cold C candidate or a renewed reserve/take capability.
+7. **R08:** whole concrete protocol review and synchronized Mortal/afterlife/daemon/helper/worker documentation, examples and source guards once emitted. The existing internal-reader no-update rationale cannot cover this new external request/control lifecycle.
+
+The 15-family future matrix is a useful design inventory. It does not yet fix executable category membership/counts, actual fixture construction, hook/transaction cut positions or complete phase oracles. Those depend on the exact owner contracts above and need independent SOURCE/FIXTURE/SELECTION review. Fresh G5/Late2/EVIDENCE remains required for subsequent source/admission/common/cleanup implementation cycles; no runtime release, full suite or unrelated passing-category repetition follows from this proposal review.
+
+## Acceptance boundary and evidence
+
+Conditional discussion of the architecture is supported, with PH-D01 correction required. Full schema/owner/worker/history implementation remains blocked by the explicit exact-design dependencies; same-root complete pre-P0 recovery is not established. Internal retention/HOLD is not public lawful recovery or permission to narrow legal outcomes. No additional pathname, automatic F2 switch, T197 implementation, new QTE or activation is selected. Full F1/T179/T182/T192/P0, D4/guided/visual/Windows/D8 remain open. Persistent user authorization is not withdrawn or made subject to another permission question; these are concrete technical design and qualification gates.
+
+The scoped four-file review covers the new proposal pair and its plan/tasks status. The full carrier also contains unrelated T197 parent-seal reports; their content and the observed-reader RED/implementation claims are excluded. The parent is the sole writer. An untracked observed-reader conformance test appeared during review and is recorded in JSON; I did not inspect or modify it or treat it as part of this candidate.
+
